tes to both binary and non-binary people (Hofman, 2012). It necessitates deeper engagement as to the politics of passing, not passing, societal assimilation and non-assimilation.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["gender-binary"],"antonyms":["non-binary"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["binariness","binarise","binarize","binarist","binarization","binit","circumbinary","duobinary","exbi-","gibi-","gigabinary","interbinary","intrabinary","kibi-","kilobinary","mebi-","megabinary","negabinary","pebi-","phinary","polybinary","protobinary","pseudobinary","quebi-","robi-","superbinary","tebi-","yobi-","zebi-"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/binary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1c954e73daec97c9e4","definition":"A state in which only two values are possible, in which something must have one value or the other.","example":"The correlation between warmth and cold is an internal one where the existence of one depends on and is defined by the other. Hence, the yin-yang binary as a correlative binary of light-shade or warmth-cold [...]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["binariness","binarise","binarize","binarist","binarization","binit","circumbinary","duobinary","exbi-","gibi-","gigabinary","interbinary","intrabinary","kibi-","kilobinary","mebi-","megabinary","negabinary","pebi-","phinary","polybinary","protobinary","pseudobinary","quebi-","robi-","superbinary","tebi-","yobi-","zebi-","binary-coded decimal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/binary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a6b659982aaba0ba01","definition":"The bijective base-2 numeral system, which uses only the digits 0 and 1.","example":"As our initial exposure to the base 10 number system consisted of learning how to count, it also makes sense that we might begin by learning how to count in binary.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["base 2"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["binariness","binarise","binarize","binarist","binarization","binit","circumbinary","duobinary","exbi-","gibi-","gigabinary","interbinary","intrabinary","kibi-","kilobinary","mebi-","megabinary","negabinary","pebi-","phinary","polybinary","protobinary","pseudobinary","quebi-","robi-","superbinary","tebi-","yobi-","zebi-","binary-coded decimal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/binary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2f67b833157422d9b1","definition":"Ellipsis of binary file.","example":"Now that you have a high-level idea of what binaries look like and how they work, you're ready to dive into a real binary format.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["non-binary","text file"],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, countable, ellipsis, uncountable","wordFamily":["binariness","binarise","binarize","binarist","binarization","binit","circumbinary","duobinary","exbi-","gibi-","gigabinary","interbinary","intrabinary","kibi-","kilobinary","mebi-","megabinary","negabinary","pebi-","phinary","polybinary","protobinary","pseudobinary","quebi-","robi-","superbinary","tebi-","yobi-","zebi-","binary-coded decimal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/binary#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ae22d93812ce361c4d","definition":"Ellipsis of binary asteroid.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, countable, ellipsis, uncountable","wordFamily":["binarines